= Overview =

PKI provides a set of CLIs to manage the lightweight CAs (LWCA).

'''Note:''' The current LWCA implementation has some limitations:
* It does not work with clone outside of IPA environment. See [https://pagure.io/dogtagpki/issue/2836 Ticket #2836].
* It does not include authority ID into some audit events. See [https://pagure.io/dogtagpki/issue/2839 Ticket #2839].

= Listing Authorities =

To list all authorities:

<pre>
$ pki -d ~/.dogtag/pki-tomcat/ca/alias -n caadmin -c Secret.123 ca-authority-find
-----------------
2 entries matched
-----------------
  Host authority: true
  Authority DN:   CN=CA Signing Certificate,OU=pki-tomcat,O=EXAMPLE
  ID:             f37225e8-b6d7-49be-abe1-6a2f5f3e0be3
  Issuer DN:      CN=CA Signing Certificate,OU=pki-tomcat,O=EXAMPLE
  Serial no:      1
  Enabled:        true
  Ready to sign:  true
  Description:    Host authority

  Authority DN:   CN=test
  ID:             4aa054e0-4742-4968-8c38-6c7b8539ceb1
  Parent ID:      f37225e8-b6d7-49be-abe1-6a2f5f3e0be3
  Issuer DN:      CN=CA Signing Certificate,OU=pki-tomcat,O=EXAMPLE
  Serial no:      7
  Enabled:        true
  Ready to sign:  true
----------------------------
